/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T08:47:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T08:47:36Z","body":"Did some quick test.\r\nFeedback:\r\n1. I think the pin button should be moved to the leftmost side. Or maybe between prev/next and history buttons.\r\n2. This button increases the minimum width of the Inspector dock, but placing this button where it is currently placed is, in my opinion, the best place this button can be.\r\n3. \"Pin\" or \"Lock\"? 🤔 IDK what will be better. [Here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115531), for example, pin button is used to pin window always-on-top (and in other software I used, pin is used to pin window always-on-top). So _if_ pinning functionality will be implemented for all editor docks, current \"Pin\" may clash with it. This is just thoughts, feel free to ignore it.\r\n\r\nSome behavior that may be not intended, but I'm not sure:\r\n1. Run game, where you have node with script.\r\n2. Select this node in remote and pin it.\r\n3. Scroll to node script (at the bottom), select \"edit\" in context menu. Inspector will stay locked.\r\n4. Stop running project. Inspector is still locked to remote object (this is intended).\r\n5. Now repeat step 3. Inspector will \"drop\" selected remote object, disable lock and select script.\r\nMost likely this is intended, right?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3858855288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3858960266","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113148#issuecomment-3858960266","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113148","id":3858960266,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mAw-K","user":{"login":"DexterF