6-04-11T10:44:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-11T10:44:37Z","body":"Hello. Can this PR's conflilcts be resolved so we can test the feature? I would like to test it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4229289252/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4542806473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113148#issuecomment-4542806473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113148","id":4542806473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDsW5yQ","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T09:26:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T09:26:04Z","body":"Sorry for being this late. Tested. Works almost as expected.\r\n\r\nFirst of all I am not sure about the pin button placement. I would expect it to be on the right side where the History or Object properties button is. Maybe it's just my specific preference but usually it's on the right side I think.\r\n\r\nOne problem with the current implementation: if you pin an object, then switch to Signals or Groups panel, and then change the currently selected object to a different one, everything there is gone (the panels become empty until you select ANY node and they get populated with the pinned object's properties again).\r\n\r\nAlso I am wondering if the locked object should change if the user explicitly tells the inspector to switch to it - for example when you choose RMB -> Inspect on a resource (for example an audio stream inside an audio stream player). If that's even possible to do. That wouldn't be a problem at all if we could open multiple docks of the same type like in Unity (you can have multiple Inspectors open at the same time so you can have one inspector pinned and another show you the currently selected object info). But that's up for debate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4542806473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4615245707","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113148#issuecomment-4615245707","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113148","id":4615245707,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABExcPiw","user":{"login":"jauwnio","id":157239827,"node_id":"U_kgDOCV9KEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157239827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio","html_url":"https://github.com/jauwnio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T17:52:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T17:52:25Z","body":"> Sorry for being this late. Tested. Works almost as expected.\r\n> \r\n> First of all I am not sure about the pin button placement. I would expect it to be on the right side where the History or Object properties button is. Maybe it's just my specific preference but usually it's on the right side I think.\r\n> \r\n> One problem with the current implementation: if you pin an object, then switch to Signals or Groups panel, and then change the currently selected object to a different one, everything there is gone (the panels become empty until you select ANY node and they get populated with the pinned object's properties again).\r\n> \r\n> Also I am wondering if the locked object should change if the user explicitly tells the inspector to switch to it - for example when you choose RMB -> Inspect on a resource (for example an audio stream inside an audio stream player). If that's even possible to do. That wouldn't be a problem at all if we could open multiple docks of the same type like in Unity (you can have multiple Inspectors open at the same time so you can have one inspector pinned and another show you the currently selected object info). But that's up for debate.\r\n\r\nI also tested this a bit today, I've been using the Inspector Lock plugin for a long time now to give me this functionality and I much prefer where the button is located in that plugin, see screenshot:\r\n<img width=\"372\" height=\"113\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e264b2b-03cf-4e38-b9d1-617772cf2c25\" />\r\n\r\nI think that matches what @romgerman was proposing\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4615245707/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]